    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the two new acceptance tests.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a read-time derived attribute of the owner response, so I followed the same pattern the codebase already uses for `locality`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (readonly string), so the generated DTO has the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the field via a MapStruct expression to a new `contactPreference(owner)` default method:\n   ```java\n   String email = owner.getEmail();\n   return (email != null && !email.isBlank()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   ```\n\nSince the mapping lives in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, every read path (`RespondWithOwner`, created/updated responders, and list endpoints) returns the field consistently. I treated a blank email the same as absent so an empty string still yields `PHONE`.",
